# Settings for a Docker host that builds containers from Dockerfiles in this repo: the site (Dockerfile path: Dockerfile,
# port 3000) and its database (deploy/db/Dockerfile, at the end of this file). Create the database first.
# Enter these in the hosting panel; never commit real values. Details: "Containers on a hosting platform" in README.md.
# All are read when the container starts: after changing one, restart the container (no rebuild needed).
# Leave the panel's entrypoint, command, init commands, UID and GID empty in both containers.

# ===== The site (Dockerfile) =====

# --- Required ---
# The database container: its name (db) is its address inside the project, and the password is its POSTGRES_PASSWORD.
# Or the host's PostgreSQL 16 (the admin's backups use PostgreSQL 16 tools; a newer server cannot be backed up);
# with the provider's own certificate add ?sslmode=no-verify. Tables are created by migrations on start.
DATABASE_URI=postgres://idp:password@db:5432/idp
# Signs editor logins. A long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`; keep it the same between deploys.
PAYLOAD_SECRET=
# Public address: canonical links, sitemap, link previews. Without it they point to http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.ru

# --- Already set in the image; override only to change them ---
# MEDIA_DIR=/data/media
# BACKUPS_DIR=/data/backup
# BACKUP_MODE=prod
# PORT=3000
# Backups kept: the newest KEEP_LAST, plus the newest of each of KEEP_MONTHLY months (see BACKUP.md)
# KEEP_LAST=14
# KEEP_MONTHLY=6

# --- Persistent volumes ---
# /data/media        uploaded photos and videos: REQUIRED, or uploads are lost on every redeploy
# /data/backup       backups made from the admin
#                    (one disk mounted at /data covers both)
# /app/.next/cache   optional, image cache (faster after restarts)
# A host set up before 2026-11-08 has its volumes at /app/media and /app/backups. Before deploying this version,
# move both mounts to the paths above, or keep them and set MEDIA_DIR=/app/media and BACKUPS_DIR=/app/backups here.

# ===== The database (deploy/db/Dockerfile) =====
# A container named db, built from this repo with the Dockerfile path deploy/db/Dockerfile (any build context).
# Its one setting, entered in that container, not the site's. openssl rand -hex 32; the same as in DATABASE_URI above:
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# Already set in its image: PGDATA=/data/db, POSTGRES_USER=idp, POSTGRES_DB=idp
# Persistent volume: one disk at /data (an SSD if offered). Without one the container stops and says so.
# Port 5432 inside the project only: no domain, no public port. Rebuild it only when deploy/db/Dockerfile changes.
